* RSpice functional parts.
*
* Each subcircuit here is a part placed from the Component shelf. They are
* written on the native special-function devices (OTA, BUF, AND, OR, XOR,
* SCHMITT, SRFLOP, COUNTER, PHASEDET, SAMPLEHOLD) and resolve by name with
* no include. Pin order and parameter names are the placement contract the
* schematic binds: change them only together with the part's descriptor.
*
* Internal stages that carry no supply current of their own are referenced to
* the global ground, so a part's supply pins carry its quiescent current and
* the current its output delivers, and nothing else. An output's current is
* steered to the positive supply pin while sourced and to the negative one
* while sunk by a split that is smooth through zero (a 1 nA knee), which keeps
* Newton away from the corner a hard max() would put there.

* Op-amp. Pins: IN+ IN- V+ V- OUT.
* A single-pole voltage-feedback amplifier: a transconductance stage driving
* a 100 pF compensation node sets GBW and AVOL, its current limit sets the
* slew rate, the node is clamped inside the supply pins by HEADROOM, and a
* current-limited output stage of resistance ROUT drives OUT. Output current
* is drawn from V+ when sourced and returned to V- when sunk. The only noise
* is the input noise EN and IN describe.
.subckt RSPICE_FN_OPAMP INP INN VP VN OUT
+ AVOL=200k GBW=10Meg SLEW=10Meg VOS=0 IB=0 IOS=0 RIN=1T CIN=2p
+ EN=10n ENK=100 IN=1f INK=0 ROUT=50 ISRC=25m ISNK=25m HEADROOM=0 IQ=1m
VOS NP INP {VOS}
IBP INP VN {IB+IOS/2}
IBN INN VN {IB-IOS/2}
RIN NP INN {RIN}
CIN NP INN {CIN}
A1 INN NP 0 0 0 0 NC 0 OTA G={2*pi*GBW*100p} IOUT={SLEW*100p} VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
+ EN={EN} ENK={ENK} IN={IN} INK={INK}
RC NC 0 {AVOL/(2*pi*GBW*100p)} NOISY=0
CC NC 0 100p
EHI NXH 0 VP 0 1
VHI NXH NHI {HEADROOM}
ELO NXL 0 VN 0 1
VLO NLO NXL {HEADROOM}
A2 NHI NHI NHI NHI NHI NHI NC NHI OTA G=0 LINEAR VHIGH=0 VLOW=-1e9 RCLAMP=1m
A3 NLO NLO NLO NLO NLO NLO NC NLO OTA G=0 LINEAR VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=0 RCLAMP=1m
A4 OUT NC 0 0 0 0 NO 0 OTA G={1/ROUT} IOUT={ISRC} ISINK={-ISNK} ASYM VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
VSNS NO OUT 0
BSRC VP 0 I=0.5*(I(VSNS)+sqrt(I(VSNS)*I(VSNS)+1e-18))
BSNK 0 VN I=0.5*(sqrt(I(VSNS)*I(VSNS)+1e-18)-I(VSNS))
IQ VP VN {IQ}
.ends RSPICE_FN_OPAMP

* Comparator. Pins: IN+ IN- V+ V- OUT.
* A differential Schmitt trigger decides; it trips HYST/2 either side of
* -VOS and changes state TPD after its input crosses, and the output edge
* then takes TRISE or TFALL to cross the full swing. The decision drives a
* push-pull stage that swings between the supply pins behind ROUT, or, with
* OC=1, an open-collector stage that only sinks toward V-.
.subckt RSPICE_FN_COMPARATOR INP INN VP VN OUT
+ VOS=0 HYST=1m TPD=100n TRISE=10n TFALL=10n OC=0 ROUT=50 ISRC=20m ISNK=20m IQ=500u
A1 INP INN 0 0 0 NLB NL 0 SCHMITT VT={-VOS} VH={HYST/2} VHIGH=1 VLOW=0 TD={TPD}
+ TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL}
EVN NVN 0 VN 0 1
A2 0 NL VP VN NVN NVN NT NVN OTA G=1 LINEAR VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
RT NT NVN 1 NOISY=0
VPP NPP 0 {1-OC}
A3 OUT NT NPP 0 0 0 NO 0 OTA G={1/ROUT} IOUT={ISRC} ISINK={-ISNK} ASYM VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
EOC NOC 0 NLB 0 {OC}
A4 OUT VN NOC 0 0 0 NO 0 OTA G={1/ROUT} IOUT={ISNK} ISINK={-ISNK} VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
VSNS NO OUT 0
BSRC VP 0 I=0.5*(I(VSNS)+sqrt(I(VSNS)*I(VSNS)+1e-18))
BSNK 0 VN I=0.5*(sqrt(I(VSNS)*I(VSNS)+1e-18)-I(VSNS))
IQ VP VN {IQ}
.ends RSPICE_FN_COMPARATOR

* Operational transconductance amplifier. Pins: IN+ IN- IABC V+ V- OUT.
* The current into IABC biases a differential pair: the output current is
* IABC*tanh((V(IN+)-V(IN-)+VOS)/VLIN), so the transconductance is IABC/VLIN
* and the output saturates at +-IABC. The inputs draw IB and IOS, are joined
* by RIN and CIN, and carry the noise EN and IN describe, as the op-amp's do:
* the pair's transconductance scales the noise with the signal, so it stays
* referred to the input at any bias. IABC sits 0.65 V above V-, rising 10 mV
* per mA beyond that, and takes no current below it. The output is a current
* loaded by ROUT and COUT, held HEADROOM inside the supply pins.
.subckt RSPICE_FN_OTA INP INN IABC VP VN OUT
+ VLIN=51.7m VOS=0 IB=0 IOS=0 RIN=1T CIN=2p EN=7n ENK=0 IN=0 INK=0 ROUT=10Meg
+ COUT=5p HEADROOM=1 IQ=1m
VOS NP INP {VOS}
IBP INP VN {IB+IOS/2}
IBN INN VN {IB-IOS/2}
RIN NP INN {RIN}
CIN NP INN {CIN}
VIA IABC NIA 0
A0 VN VN VN VN VN VN NIA VN OTA G=0 LINEAR VHIGH=0.65 VLOW=-1e9 RCLAMP=10
FIA 0 NIB VIA 1
RIB NIB 0 1 NOISY=0
A1 INN NP 0 0 0 0 NTH 0 OTA G={1/VLIN} IOUT=1 ISINK=-1 VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
+ EN={EN} ENK={ENK} IN={IN} INK={INK}
RTH NTH 0 1 NOISY=0
A2 0 NTH NIB 0 0 0 NO 0 OTA G=1 LINEAR VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
VSNS NO OUT 0
ROUT OUT 0 {ROUT}
COUT OUT 0 {COUT}
EHI NXH 0 VP 0 1
VHI NXH NHI {HEADROOM}
ELO NXL 0 VN 0 1
VLO NLO NXL {HEADROOM}
A3 NHI NHI NHI NHI NHI NHI OUT NHI OTA G=0 LINEAR VHIGH=0 VLOW=-1e9 RCLAMP=1
A4 NLO NLO NLO NLO NLO NLO OUT NLO OTA G=0 LINEAR VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=0 RCLAMP=1
BSRC VP 0 I=0.5*(I(VSNS)+sqrt(I(VSNS)*I(VSNS)+1e-18))
BSNK 0 VN I=0.5*(sqrt(I(VSNS)*I(VSNS)+1e-18)-I(VSNS))
IQ VP VN {IQ}
.ends RSPICE_FN_OTA

* Analog-threshold logic. Inputs and outputs are voltages to ground: an input
* is high at or above the midpoint of VHIGH and VLOW, an output drives VHIGH
* or VLOW behind ROUT. A change reaches the output TD later (an input pulse
* shorter than TD never does) and the edge takes TRISE or TFALL.
* The gates take five inputs. An input tied to ground is no input at all, so
* a gate drawn with fewer has the rest tied there: AND and OR read the inputs
* left, and XOR is high when exactly one of them is.
.subckt RSPICE_FN_INV A Y VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TD=10n TRISE=5n TFALL=5n ROUT=50
A1 A 0 0 0 0 Y 0 0 BUF VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} TD={TD} TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_INV
.subckt RSPICE_FN_BUF A Y VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TD=10n TRISE=5n TFALL=5n ROUT=50
A1 A 0 0 0 0 0 Y 0 BUF VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} TD={TD} TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_BUF
.subckt RSPICE_FN_AND A B C D E Y VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TD=10n TRISE=5n TFALL=5n ROUT=50
A1 A B C D E 0 Y 0 AND VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} TD={TD} TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_AND
.subckt RSPICE_FN_NAND A B C D E Y VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TD=10n TRISE=5n TFALL=5n ROUT=50
A1 A B C D E Y 0 0 AND VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} TD={TD} TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_NAND
.subckt RSPICE_FN_OR A B C D E Y VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TD=10n TRISE=5n TFALL=5n ROUT=50
A1 A B C D E 0 Y 0 OR VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} TD={TD} TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_OR
.subckt RSPICE_FN_NOR A B C D E Y VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TD=10n TRISE=5n TFALL=5n ROUT=50
A1 A B C D E Y 0 0 OR VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} TD={TD} TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_NOR
.subckt RSPICE_FN_XOR A B C D E Y VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TD=10n TRISE=5n TFALL=5n ROUT=50
A1 A B C D E 0 Y 0 XOR VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} TD={TD} TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_XOR

* Schmitt triggers: the input rises through VT+HYST/2 to switch and falls
* through VT-HYST/2 to switch back.
.subckt RSPICE_FN_SCHMITT_INV A Y VT=2.5 HYST=0.5 VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TD=10n TRISE=5n TFALL=5n
+ ROUT=50
A1 A 0 0 0 0 Y 0 0 SCHMITT VT={VT} VH={HYST/2} VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} TD={TD}
+ TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_SCHMITT_INV
.subckt RSPICE_FN_SCHMITT_BUF A Y VT=2.5 HYST=0.5 VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TD=10n TRISE=5n TFALL=5n
+ ROUT=50
A1 A 0 0 0 0 0 Y 0 SCHMITT VT={VT} VH={HYST/2} VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} TD={TD}
+ TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_SCHMITT_BUF

* 555 timer. Pins: TRIG THR RESET OUT DIS CTRL VCC GND.
* The classic block diagram: three equal RDIV resistors put CTRL at 2/3 of
* the supply and the trigger reference at 1/3 (half of CTRL when CTRL is
* driven). THR above CTRL sets the latch and TRIG below the reference clears
* it, the trigger winning when both act; RESET below 0.7 V sets it and holds
* it set. The set latch drives OUT low and turns the DIS switch on: RDIS to
* GND, passing at most IDIS. OUT swings from GND to DROP below VCC behind
* ROUT, sourcing at most ISRC and sinking at most ISNK, its edges TEDGE long.
* IQ is the quiescent current besides the divider's. The defaults are a
* bipolar 555; the part's Process preset fills in a CMOS one.
.subckt RSPICE_FN_555 TRIG THR RESET OUT DIS CTRL VCC GND
+ DROP=1.4 ROUT=5 ISRC=200m ISNK=200m TEDGE=100n IQ=3m RDIV=5k RDIS=10 IDIS=50m
R1 VCC CTRL {RDIV}
R2 CTRL NREF {RDIV}
R3 NREF GND {RDIV}
A1 THR CTRL 0 0 0 0 NTH GND SCHMITT VT=0 VH=0.1m VHIGH=1 VLOW=0 TRISE=1n
A2 NREF TRIG 0 0 0 0 NTR GND SCHMITT VT=0 VH=0.1m VHIGH=1 VLOW=0 TRISE=1n
A3 RESET GND 0 0 0 NRA NRO GND SCHMITT VT=0.7 VH=0.05 VHIGH=1 VLOW=0 TRISE=1n
A4 NTH NRA GND GND GND GND NSET GND OR VHIGH=1 VLOW=0 TRISE=1n
A5 NTR NRO GND GND GND GND NCLR GND AND VHIGH=1 VLOW=0 TRISE=1n
A6 NSET NCLR GND GND GND NQB NQ GND SRFLOP VHIGH=1 VLOW=0 TRISE={TEDGE}
EG NG 0 GND 0 1
EHI NXH 0 VCC 0 1
VHI NXH NHI {DROP}
A7 0 NQB NHI GND NG NG NT NG OTA G=1 LINEAR VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
RT NT NG 1 NOISY=0
A8 OUT NT 0 0 0 0 NO 0 OTA G={1/ROUT} IOUT={ISRC} ISINK={-ISNK} ASYM VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
VSNS NO OUT 0
BSRC VCC 0 I=0.5*(I(VSNS)+sqrt(I(VSNS)*I(VSNS)+1e-18))
BSNK 0 GND I=0.5*(sqrt(I(VSNS)*I(VSNS)+1e-18)-I(VSNS))
A9 DIS GND NQ GND GND GND DIS GND OTA G={1/RDIS} IOUT={IDIS} ISINK={-IDIS} VHIGH=1e9 VLOW=-1e9
IQ VCC GND {IQ}
.ends RSPICE_FN_555

* Phase-frequency detector. Pins: A B OUT.
* A rising edge on A steps the state up and one on B steps it down, between
* -1 and +1; OUT sources IOUT times the state, held between VLOW and VHIGH.
.subckt RSPICE_FN_PHASEDET A B OUT IOUT=100u VTH=2.5 VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 ROUT=1G
A1 A B 0 0 0 0 OUT 0 PHASEDET IOUT={IOUT} REF={VTH} VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_PHASEDET

* Divide-by-N counter. Pins: CLK RST OUT.
* Counts rising CLK edges modulo N; OUT is high for the first DUTY*N counts
* of each cycle. RST high holds the count at zero.
.subckt RSPICE_FN_COUNTER CLK RST OUT N=2 DUTY=0.5 VHIGH=5 VLOW=0 TRISE=5n TFALL=5n
+ ROUT=50
A1 CLK RST 0 0 0 0 OUT 0 COUNTER CYCLES={N} DUTY={DUTY} VHIGH={VHIGH} VLOW={VLOW}
+ TRISE={TRISE} TFALL={TFALL} ROUT={ROUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_COUNTER

* Sample and hold. Pins: IN SAMPLE OUT.
* While SAMPLE is above VTH the output tracks IN; when it falls the output
* holds the last value, driven through ROUT into COUT.
.subckt RSPICE_FN_SAMPLEHOLD IN SAMPLE OUT VTH=2.5 ROUT=1 COUT=10p
A1 IN 0 0 SAMPLE 0 0 OUT 0 SAMPLEHOLD REF={VTH} ROUT={ROUT}
COUT OUT 0 {COUT}
.ends RSPICE_FN_SAMPLEHOLD
